              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for siblings, then the French for large family."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la grossesse",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la grossesse — \"pregnancy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pendant sa grossesse, elle a continué à travailler. During her pregnancy she kept on working."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Être enceinte — to be pregnant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la grossesse is built on gros \"big\" with -esse; gros is inherited from Late Latin grossus \"thick\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
